{
    "description": "Some trigonomic approximations: cos, sin, tan, arctan, © 2001 The Ganssle Group. Approximations are faster than library functions but less accurate. You should be careful using approximations - they can break your code. In evieve all approximations are tested to work on the code in which they are used. Note, in this 'evi_trig' GenExpr code, in terms of cos/sin CPU savings, only '73' or lower are worthwhile, for 121 or higher there is no point over library cos/sin. See the source code for more (commented out) code if you are interested.",
